      "Reading Notes 7.2–7.5",
      "<p>Coulomb’s law: attraction grows with nuclear charge and shrinks with distance, and each electron is also repelled by the others. So Z<sub>eff</sub> is always less than the actual nuclear charge. Ions with the same charge get larger down a group. An isoelectronic series (O<sup>2−</sup>, F<sup>−</sup>, Na<sup>+</sup>, Mg<sup>2+</sup>, Al<sup>3+</sup>, all 10 electrons) shrinks as protons increase. Cations lose electrons from the highest n first (4s before 3d); anions add to the lowest open n. Ionization energy rises for each successive electron.</p>"
